Z||000000||DecadenceR||07-07-2001||12:00 AM||||Okay. Heres the deal.<BR>You know when you drive over those large metal grates on a bridge? And your tires make a weird noise and the steering feels weird until you get back on the pavement? Think about that sound and feel for a minute...<BR>When I drive and I hit any kind of bump or dip, or ANYTHING that makes the suspension move, when the suspension goes downward, it makes a noise and feel similar to this. It happens when the suspension is down, and only on accelertion or constant speed. If I hit a bump while braking, it doesn't do it. It sounds and feels like it's coming from the right half of the car, possibly the front, but I can't tell for sure.<BR>Anyone have an idea?<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SigPic.jpg"> <BR>AIM - DecadenceR||||reg||1
